    "body": "claim released: the claim comment of 2026-11-25T02:00:44Z is a duplicate. A second session with the same name claimed this issue at 01:59:06Z, 98 seconds earlier. PR #3957 is the PR of this issue. I opened no second PR and changed nothing on #3957 or its branch.\n\nThe second session did the work before it saw the first claim. The held work is on `mkinney:issue/3332-wire-exit-pick-alt` (head `02d34906a`, contains `upstream/main` `d94b9816d`). Use it or drop it; the maintainer and the author of #3957 decide.\n\nDifferences from #3957 that can help its rework:\n\n| Subject | PR #3957 | Held branch |\n|---|---|---|\n| Closed profile, after the lap | The lead-out goes to the pick. The path does not return to the threading point. | The wire travels in its kerf (the shorter way) to the nearest point of the path to the pick. The lead-out returns to the threading point. The path starts and ends at the threading point, as each wire path does today. |\n| Tabs | An exit pick with tabs is refused by name. | The stretch that holds the exit is cut last and left there, before the tab cut-off. The cut-off moves do not change. An exit on a tab is refused by name. |\n| Posted program | A test reads the posted text for the block at the pick. | `an_exit_cut_posts_the_golden_program_with_one_more_block` compares the whole program: it is `wire_slug_punch.nc` plus the one block `G1 X-20.165 Y8.`. |\n| Refusal of the other cuts | At the command door and at generation. | At generation only. |\n\nFacts about the held branch:\n\n- It has the same blocker as #3957. `egui_app::start_exit_rows::tests::the_wire_geometry_tab_groups_the_start_hole_and_says_the_exit_is_not_taken` fails on it (`cargo xtask gate test ... --crate ui`: 1 failed). It has no Exit point row on the Wire Contour page.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 351 steps, 0 failed, on `af2de890b`. That plan has no `camcraft-ui` lib step, so it did not show the UI failure.\n- On the head `02d34906a`: 22 wire, golden and catalog suites, 0 failed. Clippy for `camcraft-motion` and `camcraft-app` is clean. No `.nc` or `.cl` file changed.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main` on `02d34906a`: 106 steps, 1 failed. The failed step is `app heavy: pocket3d_hsm` with counts `(4688, 4660, 1980)`. That is #3886, red on `main`.\n- 12 mutations, each red, each restored.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/3332-wire-exit-pick.md` on the held branch.\n\nI did not change the labels. The issue stays `in-review` with PR #3957.\n",
